          %h2#references References
          %p The original article is
          %ul
            %li#Artin23
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emil+Artin"}> Emil Artin
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %em Über eine neue Art von L Reihen
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#Snyder02"} Snyder 02, section A
          %p Reviews include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artin_L-function"} Artin L-function
            %li#MurtyMurty12
              %p
                M. Ram Murty, V. Kumar Murty,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Non-vanishing of L-functions and applications
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.beck-shop.de/fachbuch/leseprobe/9783034802734_Excerpt_001.pdf"} chapter 2 pdf
            %li#Snyder02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noah+Snyder"}> Noah Snyder
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Artin L-Functions: A Historical Approach
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.columbia.edu/~nsnyder/thesismain.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and in the context of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Langlands+program"} Langlands program
          %ul
            %li#Gelbhart84
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Gelbart"}> Stephen Gelbart
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em An elementary introduction to the Langlands program
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/journals/bull/1984-10-02/S0273-0979-1984-15237-6/"} web
          %p Further development includes
          %ul
            %li#RamMurty94
              M. Ram Murty,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Selberg’s conjectures and Artin -functions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/journals/bull/1994-31-01/S0273-0979-1994-00479-3/home.html"} web
          %p
            The analogy with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Selberg+zeta+function"} Selberg zeta function
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Brown09
              %p
                Darin Brown,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lifting properties of prime geodesics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.rmjm/1239113439"} euclid
            %li#Morishita12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masanori+Morishita"}> Masanori Morishita
                , section 12.1 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Knots and Primes: An Introduction to Arithmetic Topology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=DOnkGOTnI78C&pg=PA156#v=onepage&q&f=false"} web
          %p The analogies between Alexander polynomial and L-functions and touched upon in
          %ul
            %li
              Ken-ichi Sugiyama,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The properties of an L-function from a geometric point of view
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "http://geoquant2007.mi.ras.ru/sugiyama.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  A topological
                  %math#mathml_12049cb8a6825b151e4c22a4db78dcd7f06ef271_46.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
